    "image": "/images/blog/public_ip.png",
    "content": "![pbs-screenshot](/images/blog/public_ip.png)\n\nQuickly Check Your Public IP💡\n\nIf you’re hosting services at home like Home Assistant, a media server, or a private cloud it’s often useful to know your current public IP address. Instead of logging into your router or using a browser, just run this in your terminal:\n\n```bash\ncurl https://ipinfo.io/ip\n```\n\nDo you use small commands like this in your homelab?",
